abstract: >-
  Final project (group 5) of the course Neural Networks & Deep Learning Foundations
  (MSA-DATB09-91), Albert School, 2026-27. A guide for a fictional French fine-arts museum that
  recognises the genre or style of a painting from a photo, tells a short story of that tradition,
  and answers questions in natural language. It compares a classical baseline, a feed-forward
  network, a fine-tuned ResNet-18 and CLIP, and measures how solid, calibrated and costly each is.
repository-code: "https://github.com/loubrnt/museum-guide-deep-learning"
keywords:
  - deep learning
  - image classification
  - CLIP
  - WikiArt
  - museum
